---
import BaseHead from '../components/BaseHead.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';

const title = 'Single-Agent vs Multi-Agent Architectures';
const description =
	'A research narrative on what recent evidence says about single-agent and multi-agent LLM system architecture.';
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
	<head>
		<BaseHead title={title} description={description} />
		<style>
			:root {
				--ink: #16202a;
				--muted: #596774;
				--line: #d8e0e6;
				--paper: #ffffff;
				--wash: #f5f7f7;
				--blue: #2a78d6;
				--aqua: #1baf7a;
				--gold: #a27517;
				--red: #d03b3b;
				--green: #23715b;
			}

			body {
				background: #ffffff;
				color: var(--ink);
			}

			main {
				width: 100%;
				max-width: none;
				margin: 0;
				padding: 0;
			}

			.wrap {
				width: min(100% - 2rem, 1180px);
				margin: 0 auto;
			}

			section {
				border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line);
			}

			.hero {
				padding: 4.5rem 0 3.5rem;
				background: linear-gradient(180deg, #f7faf9 0%, #ffffff 78%);
			}

			.kicker,
			.eyebrow {
				margin: 0 0 0.75rem;
				color: var(--green);
				font-size: 0.88rem;
				font-weight: 700;
				text-transform: uppercase;
			}

			h1,
			h2,
			h3,
			p {
				margin: 0;
			}

			h1 {
				max-width: 840px;
				font-size: clamp(2.45rem, 5vw, 4.6rem);
				line-height: 1.02;
			}

			h2 {
				max-width: 940px;
				font-size: clamp(1.8rem, 3.4vw, 2.9rem);
				line-height: 1.08;
			}

			h3 {
				font-size: 1.14rem;
				line-height: 1.3;
			}

			.lede {
				max-width: 780px;
				margin-top: 1.4rem;
				color: var(--muted);
				font-size: clamp(1.08rem, 1.8vw, 1.26rem);
				line-height: 1.58;
			}

			.thesis {
				max-width: 820px;
				margin-top: 1.6rem;
				padding: 1.1rem 1.2rem;
				border-left: 5px solid var(--green);
				background: #eef7f3;
				color: #173d32;
				font-size: 1.02rem;
				line-height: 1.55;
			}

			.nav {
				position: sticky;
				top: 3.35rem;
				z-index: 4;
				background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.93);
				border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
				border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line);
				backdrop-filter: blur(14px);
			}

			.nav .wrap {
				display: flex;
				gap: 0.45rem;
				overflow-x: auto;
				padding: 0.7rem 0;
			}

			.nav a {
				flex: 0 0 auto;
				padding: 0.5rem 0.75rem;
				border-radius: 999px;
				color: var(--ink);
				font-size: 0.9rem;
				line-height: 1;
				text-decoration: none;
			}

			.nav a:hover {
				background: #edf3f8;
				color: var(--blue);
			}

			.block {
				padding: 4.2rem 0;
				scroll-margin-top: 7rem;
			}

			.block.alt {
				background: var(--wash);
			}

			.section-head {
				display: grid;
				gap: 0.9rem;
				margin-bottom: 1.6rem;
			}

			.section-head p {
				max-width: 820px;
				color: var(--muted);
				font-size: 1.04rem;
				line-height: 1.55;
			}

			.prose {
				display: grid;
				gap: 1rem;
				max-width: 920px;
			}

			.prose p {
				color: var(--ink);
				font-size: 1.06rem;
				line-height: 1.65;
			}

			.takeaway {
				max-width: 920px;
				margin-top: 1.3rem;
				padding: 1rem 1.1rem;
				border-left: 5px solid var(--gold);
				background: #fff8ea;
				color: #4f3b11;
				font-size: 1rem;
				line-height: 1.55;
			}

			/* figures & charts */
			.fig {
				margin: 1.8rem 0;
				padding: 1.2rem 1.25rem 1rem;
				border: 1px solid var(--line);
				border-radius: 12px;
				background: var(--paper);
			}

			.fig .fig-title {
				font-size: 1.05rem;
				font-weight: 650;
				color: var(--ink);
			}

			.fig .fig-sub {
				margin-top: 0.25rem;
				color: var(--muted);
				font-size: 0.92rem;
				line-height: 1.45;
			}

			.chart {
				width: 100%;
				height: auto;
				display: block;
				margin-top: 0.6rem;
				font-family: inherit;
			}

			figure {
				margin: 0;
			}

			figcaption {
				margin-top: 0.7rem;
				padding-top: 0.6rem;
				border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
				color: var(--muted);
				font-size: 0.9rem;
				line-height: 1.5;
			}

			/* stat tiles */
			.tiles {
				display: grid;
				grid-template-columns: repeat(4, minmax(0, 1fr));
				gap: 1rem;
				margin: 1.8rem 0;
			}

			.tile {
				padding: 1.05rem 1.15rem;
				border: 1px solid var(--line);
				border-radius: 12px;
				background: var(--paper);
			}

			.tile .val {
				color: var(--ink);
				font-size: 1.85rem;
				font-weight: 650;
				line-height: 1.15;
			}

			.tile .lab {
				margin-top: 0.45rem;
				color: var(--muted);
				font-size: 0.88rem;
				line-height: 1.45;
			}

			/* card grids (defects, topologies, sources) */
			.cards {
				display: grid;
				grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr));
				gap: 1rem;
				margin: 1.8rem 0;
			}

			.topos {
				display: grid;
				grid-template-columns: repeat(5, minmax(0, 1fr));
				gap: 1rem;
				margin: 1.8rem 0;
			}

			.card {
				padding: 1.05rem 1.1rem;
				border: 1px solid var(--line);
				border-radius: 12px;
				background: var(--paper);
			}

			.card h3 {
				margin-bottom: 0.45rem;
				font-size: 1rem;
			}

			.card p {
				color: var(--muted);
				font-size: 0.92rem;
				line-height: 1.52;
			}

			.card .mini {
				width: 100%;
				height: auto;
				margin-bottom: 0.55rem;
			}

			.card .quote {
				margin-top: 0.55rem;
				padding-left: 0.7rem;
				border-left: 3px solid var(--line);
				font-style: italic;
			}

			/* DPI theory box */
			.dpi {
				display: grid;
				gap: 0.6rem;
				max-width: 920px;
				margin: 1.8rem 0;
				padding: 1.2rem 1.3rem;
				border: 1px solid var(--line);
				border-radius: 12px;
				background: var(--paper);
			}

			.dpi .chain {
				display: flex;
				flex-wrap: wrap;
				align-items: center;
				gap: 0.6rem;
				font-size: 1rem;
			}

			.dpi .box {
				padding: 0.5rem 0.8rem;
				border: 1.5px solid var(--blue);
				border-radius: 8px;
				color: var(--ink);
				background: #eef4fc;
			}

			.dpi .box.dim {
				border-color: var(--line);
				background: var(--wash);
			}

			.dpi .arrow {
				color: var(--muted);
				font-size: 0.9rem;
			}

			.dpi .ineq {
				font-size: 1.12rem;
				color: var(--ink);
				font-weight: 600;
			}

			.dpi p {
				color: var(--muted);
				font-size: 0.94rem;
				line-height: 1.55;
			}

			/* tables */
			.table-wrap {
				width: 100%;
				overflow-x: auto;
				border: 1px solid var(--line);
				border-radius: 8px;
				background: #ffffff;
				margin-top: 1.4rem;
			}

			table {
				width: 100%;
				min-width: 680px;
				border-collapse: collapse;
				font-size: 0.93rem;
				line-height: 1.4;
			}

			th,
			td {
				padding: 0.85rem;
				border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line);
				text-align: left;
				vertical-align: top;
			}

			th {
				background: #eef3f0;
				color: #25362f;
				font-size: 0.82rem;
				text-transform: uppercase;
			}

			tr:last-child td {
				border-bottom: 0;
			}

			.closing {
				background: #10251f;
				color: #ffffff;
			}

			.closing h2,
			.closing h3 {
				color: #ffffff;
			}

			.closing .section-head p,
			.closing .card p {
				color: #dce8e3;
			}

			.closing .card {
				border-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.22);
				background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.08);
			}

			.closing a {
				color: #aee4d1;
			}

			a {
				text-underline-offset: 0.18em;
			}

			@media (max-width: 980px) {
				.tiles,
				.cards {
					grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
				}

				.topos {
					grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr));
				}
			}

			@media (max-width: 680px) {
				.hero,
				.block {
					padding: 3rem 0;
				}

				.tiles,
				.cards,
				.topos {
					grid-template-columns: 1fr;
				}
			}
		</style>
	</head>
	<body>
		<Header />
		<main>
			<section class="hero" id="top">
				<div class="wrap">
					<p class="kicker">A research story · three papers, 2025–2026</p>
					<h1>What actually scales when we add more agents?</h1>
					<p class="lede">
						The intuition is that several LLM agents should beat one: split the
						work across roles, hypotheses, tools, debate rounds, or independent
						samples. Three recent studies show a more conditional picture —
						coordination can improve, match, or degrade a strong single agent
						depending on task structure, model capability, and whether the extra
						compute is even being counted.
					</p>
					<p class="thesis">
						The central question is not "do more agents help?" but <strong>when
						explicit coordination changes the execution graph in a useful
						way</strong>. The three studies tighten that question in order: cost
						first (Gao et al.), then topology (Kim et al.), then budget-controlled
						information flow (Tran &amp; Kiela).
					</p>
				</div>
			</section>

			<nav class="nav" aria-label="page sections">
				<div class="wrap">
					<a href="#hybrid">When teams get costly</a>
					<a href="#scaling">When topology matters</a>
					<a href="#budget">When budget is fixed</a>
					<a href="#agenda">Open questions</a>
					<a href="#sources">Sources</a>
				</div>
			</nav>

			<!-- ============ PAPER 1: Gao et al. ============ -->
			<section class="block alt" id="hybrid">
				<div class="wrap">
					<div class="section-head">
						<p class="eyebrow">Act 1 · May 2025 · the deployment pressure test</p>
						<h2>Single-agent or Multi-agent Systems? Why Not Both?</h2>
						<p>
							Gao et al. (UIUC) enter from the systems side: 9 MAS frameworks,
							15 datasets, 7 task categories, each MAS compared against a
							single-agent ablation given the whole task. If frontier single
							agents keep improving at long-context reasoning and tool use, does
							the old reason for defaulting to MAS still hold?
						</p>
					</div>

					<div class="fig">
						<figure>
							<div class="fig-title">Figure 1 · The MAS advantage is evaporating as base models improve</div>
							<div class="fig-sub">Same framework, same dataset — re-run with a modern base model. The gap that motivated multi-agent designs shrinks from +8–16 points to under 3.</div>
