							<figcaption>
								Gao et al., Table 4, Gemini-2.0-Flash. The abstract's headline is
								"+1.1–12% accuracy, up to 88% cost reduction" — the GSM8K column is
								where the 88% lives: 1,056 tokens/request vs 8,837 for always-MAS,
								with <em>higher</em> accuracy than either pure system. The caveat:
								cascades need a cheap correctness check (pass@1, exact-match);
								open-ended tasks still lack that verifier.
