			<!-- ============ PAPER 2: Kim et al. ============ -->
			<section class="block" id="scaling">
				<div class="wrap">
					<div class="section-head">
						<p class="eyebrow">Act 2 · December 2025 · the controlled scaling attempt</p>
						<h2>Towards a Science of Scaling Agent Systems</h2>
						<p>
							Kim et al. ask whether coordination can be made predictive rather
							than anecdotal: 260 configurations, five architectures, six agentic
							benchmarks, three model families at three capability tiers each,
							with prompts, tools, reasoning budgets (≈4,800 tokens/trial) and
							iteration caps standardized — so topology is the only thing that
							varies.
						</p>
					</div>

