								Tran &amp; Kiela, Table 1. Left: on DeepSeek-R1-70B / MuSiQue 4-hop,
								SAS dominates every MAS variant at every budget ≥ 500 — the paper's
								aggregate claim is that SAS is the best system or statistically
								indistinguishable from the best at all budgets except 100 tokens.
								Right: Gemini-2.5-Pro / FRAMES looks like a MAS counterexample at
								low budgets (Sequential 0.654 vs SAS 0.368 at 100 tokens); the
								paper's Appendix G attributes this to a measurement artifact — at low
								requested budgets a MAS's multiple calls surface more actual
								reasoning than a single call, so matched <em>requested</em> budgets
								are not matched compute (shaded region). Also note how early returns
								diminish: the 1k–2k numbers are already close to the 10k numbers.
							</figcaption>
